.TH HEE 1 "2026-02-15" "HEE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hee \- Human Execution Engine command dispatcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hee
[\fBhelp\fR]
.br
.B hee
\fIsubcommand\fR [\fIargs...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hee
dispatches to installed HEE tools. Runtime truth is the installed toolchain under
\fB~/.hee/bin\fR (or a repo-local prefix during test-drive).
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
Built-in:
.TP
.B help
Show help. Works after any verb, and nothing to the right of it is executed.
.TP
.B list
List every available subcommand, built-in and extension.
.TP
.B lint
Validate HEE object envelopes.
.TP
.B "hooks install"
Install this repo's git hooks.
.TP
.B "git merge"
Mass review/approve/merge open PRs.
.TP
.B "ssh send-keys"
Distribute SSH keys between hosts.
.TP
.B "contract review"
Review contract objects.
.SH EXTENSIONS
Any executable named
.I hee\-<cmd>
in the target repo's
.I tooling/bin
or the tool repo's, resolved in that order \(em so
.B hee check
runs
.IR tooling/bin/hee\-check .
Run
.B hee list
for the current set; it is derived from what is installed, not from a list
kept here.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.hee/bin
Installed truth for the toolchain.
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/bash-completion/completions/hee
Bash completion file (if installed/loaded).
